{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_3dbdb0cadd014a578331f49f","toolName":"subagent","args":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 16\nRecent Green phase: computePremium now does base * 1.1 + 5 (first insurance + fee).\n\nImplementation:\n```\nexport const computePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  _customer: Customer,\n  _quoteIndex: number,\n): number => {\n  const base = computeBasePremium(items);\n  const firstInsurance = base * 0.1;\n  return Math.ceil(base + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n```\n\nNote: this implementation already does not match the empty-list test perfectly (it computes Math.ceil(0+0+5)=5, which is correct, so it still passes).\n\nRefactor while keeping tests green. Do NOT implement ahead for per-item cursed/enchantment modifiers, loyalty discount, follow-up discount, claim/scenario logic.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 16 tests are passing. Let me now evaluate the current code and plan the refactoring.\n\n**Naming Evaluation** (first priority):\n- `computePremium` — clearly named, fits purpose\n- `firstInsurance` — good name, references the spec term \"first insurance surcharge\"\n- The comment `// Hardcoded: 1 sword (100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee = 115).` is now **misleading**: the function works for any items, not just one sword. This comment was a TDD artifact from the very first test and should be removed.\n\n**Initial APP Mass Calculation**:\n```typescript\nexport const computePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  _customer: Customer,\n  _quoteIndex: number,\n): number => {\n  // Hardcoded: 1 sword (100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee = 115).\n  const base = computeBasePremium(items);\n  const firstInsurance = base * 0.1;\n  return Math.ceil(base + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n```\n\n- Constants: `0.1`, `PROCESSING_FEE` = **2**\n- Bindings: