pt\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\n// ...\nexport const computePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  _customer: Customer,\n  _quoteIndex: number,\n): number => {\n  const base = computeBasePremium(items);\n  return Math.ceil(base * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE) + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n```\n\nNew mass:\n- Constants: `FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE`, `PROCESSING_FEE` = 2\n- Bindings: `items`, `_customer`, `_quoteIndex`, `base` = 4\n- Invocations: `computeBasePremium(...)`, `1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE`, `base * (...)`, `(...) + PROCESSING_FEE`, `Math.ceil(...)` = 5\n- Conditionals: 0\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0\n- **Total: 2 + 4 + 5×2 + 0 + 0 + 0 = 16**\n\nMass: 23 -> 16, reduction of 7.\n\nThis also matches the spec language: \"base * 1.1 + 5\" - the user already described it this way!\n\nLet me apply the refactor.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"All 16 tests are passing. Let me now evaluate the current code and plan the refactoring.\n\n**Naming Evaluation** (first priority):\n- `computePremium` — clearly named, fits purpose\n- `firstInsurance` — good name, references the spec term \"first insurance surcharge\"\n- The comment `// Hardcoded: 1 sword (100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee = 115).` is now **misleading**: the function works for any items, not just one sword. This comment was a TDD artifact from the very first test and should be removed.\n\n**Initial APP Mass Calculation**:\n```typescript\nexport const computePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  _customer: Customer,\n  _quoteIndex: number,\n): number => {\n  // Hardcoded: 1 sword (100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee = 115).\n  const base = computeBasePremium(items);\n  const firstInsurance = base * 0.1;\n  return Math.ceil(base + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n```\n\n- Constants: `0.1`, `PROCESSING_FEE` = **2**\n- Bindings: `items`, `_customer`, `_quoteIndex`, `base`, `firstInsurance` = **5**\n- Invocations: `computeBasePremium`, `base * 0.1`, `base + firstInsurance`, `firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE`, `Math.ceil` = **5** → mass 10\n- Conditionals: **0**\n- Loops: **0**\n- Assignments: `firstInsurance = base * 0.1` = **1** → mass 6\n\n**Total Mass: 2 + 5 + 10 + 0 + 0 + 6 = 23**\n\n**Applying Simple Design Rules**:\n\n- **Rule 1 (Tests Pass)**: 16/16 passing. ✓\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: The `0.1` literal is opaque — extracting it as a named constant `FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE` makes the intent self-evident. Also, the outdated \"Hardcoded: 1 sword\" comment misleads future readers.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: No duplication in this function.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: `firstInsurance` is used only once and can be folded into the formula. The spec language is `base * 1.1 + 5`, so collapsing to `base * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE) + PROCESSING_FEE` matches the spec mental model exactly and removes a redundant binding.\n\n**Refactoring Plan**:\n1. Add `FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1` near `PROCESSING_FEE` for symmetry\n2. Collapse `firstInsurance` binding into the formula\n3. Remove the misleading \"Hardcoded: 1 sword\" comment\n\nLet me apply these:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_36c488f940344a2489387caf","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"// Flat processing fee charged on every quote, on top of any per-item premium.\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\n// First insurance adds 10% on top of the base premium for every item.\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;","oldText":"// Flat processing fee charged on every quote, on top of any per-item premium.\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;"},{"newText":"export const computePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  _customer: Customer,\n  _quoteIndex: number,\n): number => {\n  const base = computeBasePremium(items);\n  return Math.ceil(base * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE) + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};","oldText":"export const computePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  _customer: Customer,\n  _quoteIndex: number,\n): number => {\n  // Hardcoded: 1 sword (100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee = 115).\n  const base = computeBasePremium(items);\n  const firstInsurance = base * 0.1;\n  return Math.ceil(base + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-58-53_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":306,"output":1779,"cacheRead":14080,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":805,"totalTokens":16165,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784926239484,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-78ca51d9-f46d-4e98-a2ff-1a71c301280d","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_36c488f940344a2489387caf","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 2 block(s) in /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-58-53_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3/src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  74 \n  75 // Flat processing fee charged on every quote, on top of any per-item premium.\n  76 const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n  77 \n+ 78 // First insurance adds 10% on top of the base premium for every item.\n+ 79 const FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\n+ 80 \n  78 // Per-type base premium for a component type: a full block of COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n  79 // costs the block premium; otherwise each component costs COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM.\n  80 const componentBasePremium = (count: number): number =>\n  81   count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n     ...\n 113   items: Item[],\n 114   _customer: Customer,\n 115   _quoteIndex: number,\n 116 ): number => {\n-117   // Hardcoded: 1 sword (100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee = 115).\n 118   const base = computeBasePremium(items);\n-119   const firstInsurance = base * 0.1;\n-120   return Math.ceil(base + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE);\n+121   return Math.ceil(base * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE