nstant `FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE` makes the intent self-evident. Also, the outdated \"Hardcoded: 1 sword\" comment misleads future readers.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: No duplication in this function.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: `firstInsurance` is used only once and can be folded into the formula. The spec language is `base * 1.1 + 5`, so collapsing to `base * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE) + PROCESSING_FEE` matches the spec mental model exactly and removes a redundant binding.\n\n**Refactoring Plan**:\n1. Add `FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1` near `PROCESSING_FEE` for symmetry\n2. Collapse `firstInsurance` binding into the formula\n3. Remove the misleading \"Hardcoded: 1 sword\" comment\n\nLet me apply these:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_36c488f940344a2489387caf","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"// Flat processing fee charged on every quote, on top of any per-item premium.\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\n// First insurance adds 10% on top of the base premium for every item.\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;","oldText":"// Flat processing fee charged on every quote, on top of any per-item premium.\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;"},{"newText":"export const computePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  _customer: Customer,\n  _quoteIndex: number,\n): number => {\n  const base = computeBasePremium(items);\n  return Math.ceil(base * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE) + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};","oldText":"export const computePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  _customer: Customer,\n  _quoteIndex: number,\n): number => {\n  // Hardcoded: 1 sword (100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee = 115).\n  const base = computeBasePremium(items);\n  const firstInsurance = base * 0.1;\n  return Math.ceil(base + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-58-53_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":3